==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*swait-'', from Indo-European ''*swoid-''.

Cognate with Old Saxon ''swêt'' (Dutch [[zweet]]), Old High German [[sweiz]] (German [[Schweiß]] ‘sweat’), Old Norse [[sveiti]] ‘sweat, blood’ (Swedish [[svett]], Danish [[sved]]), Sanskrit {{term|स्वेद|sc=Deva|tr=sveda|lang=sa}}.  The IE root also gave Latin [[sudor]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/swa:t/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
